From d5209769db8b749b2fef9e64700e8b696f38f543 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:11:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: poll the MMA consensus feed so weekly runs land within
 a minute
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An open board kept showing the pre-push grades long after MMA_Engine's
weekly run finished: the feed was cached for 15 minutes in memory, and the
request underneath it was a plain GET that GitHub Pages' CDN and the browser
HTTP cache were both free to answer from a stale copy.

Every request is now cache-busted and no-store, the in-memory TTL is a
minute, and the board polls the feed on the same cadence as the slate — but
only re-scores when generated_at actually moves, so an unchanged feed costs
one small fetch and no re-render. A fight the feed has dropped resets to its
price-only score instead of holding a stale swing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ko7MvVdXhjZNR67gyhzZq3
